id: pm-beads-ur0e
title: Keep plain-shell heredoc indentation significant
description: "Fix Greptile PR 88 finding 3890157387: non-YAML shell text inherits opener indentation as a synthetic normalization prefix."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-30T18:21:12.209Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-30T18:30:45.581Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-30T18:30:45.163Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-30T18:30:45.163Z"
author: pi-agent
severity: high
repro_steps: Indented plain-shell <<EOF opener followed by an indented EOF body line closes suppression before FLAG=--provenance.
resolution: Use an empty normalization prefix outside detected YAML block scalars and preserve all ordinary-shell indentation.
expected_result: Only YAML block indentation is removed; ordinary shell heredoc whitespace remains significant.
actual_result: Fallback opener indentation is stripped from plain shell body lines.
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-30T18:30:44.316Z",pi-agent,"Greptile 3890157387 reproduced: source-only revert stripped the indented plain-shell opener prefix, exposed FLAG=--provenance, and failed the focused regression; SOURCE_ONLY_REVERT_EXIT=1. Restored source normalizes only detected YAML block indentation. Generic heredoc fixtures now use literal unindented shell text. npm test, 100% coverage, docstring, and release:check pass."
